Station Gokana-street, Bori Metropolis, consists of a five-layer subsurface model. The resistivity profile begins at 1420 ohm-m, decreases to 859 ohm-m in the second layer, and then increases progressively through the third (987 ohm-m) and fourth (2246 ohm-m) layers, reaching a high-resistivity basement of 34337 ohm-m. 

Following the curve-type notation rules, the three-layer groupings are H (1420-859-987), A (859-987-2246), and A (987-2246-34337). Therefore, the vertical electrical sounding (VES) curve is classified as HAA. This classification is consistent with the survey interpretation currently on file.

